On Sun, Nov 27, 2011 at 04:42:17AM +0000, Matt Turner wrote:
> Hardly worth it. There's no upgrade for a PWS that's going to make it fast.

Fast is relative.  Besides, if nearly tripling the amount of RAM in my
system can eliminate even a little of the paging I'm seeing during
larger package builds, the build times will decrease by a non-trivial
(if unquantifiable) amount.  I *might* be able to get my hands on a few
SN-MSP01-HF equivalents (2x256MB kits: PC66 ECC unregistered unbuffered)
for as little as US$25 each.  That doesn't strike me as unreasonable if
the goal is to make the hardware I've got as useful as possible in the
context of the time I'm putting in on the Debian Alpha port.

Now, whether any of us should be spending any time on the Alpha port is
another matter entirely.  At least it keeps us off the streets :-).

--Bob



